Here is a script that denies access to a website or service:
```
// Deny access to a website or service
if (request.url.path === '/construction') {
 response.status = 403;
 response.statusText = 'Access denied';
 response.end();
}
```
This script uses the `if` statement to check if the URL path of the incoming request is `/construction`. If it is, the script sets the HTTP status code to 403 (Forbidden) and the status text
